  <prompt>Finish the parts of the Worklist that waited on task 154: the D-111 disposition picker on the inquiry-outcome To Do, the rule sentence in the decision wizard, and the Not filed order fixture.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE front-end developer.</role>
  <goal>The "Record the outcome of the budget inquiry" To Do in the Worklist offers the four-way disposition and records it; the wizard shows the rule's sentence.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>059 notes: `notes/059-worklist-widget.md`. Contracts: 154's `GET /api/v1/inquiries/for-todo/{todoId}` and route fields (`subjectRecordType`, `subjectRecordId`, `sentence`), and 071's `POST /api/v1/inquiries/{serviceRequestId}/disposition` (`notes/071-disposition-accrual.md` L34: body, 200/404/403/409 reason codes). Issues #1958, #1959.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/worklistService.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/worklistWizardItem.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/WorklistWidget.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-15">Scope: no Dataverse read from the widget; the inquiry and replies come only from 154's GET. The v5 derivation stays on the server.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-111">Scope: the picker shows only on a Do-lane To Do whose `subjectRecordType` is the To Do table and whose lookup returns a service request; four options with their option values (Write-off 100000000, Budget Revised 100000001, Scope Approved 100000002, No Action 100000003); the reply to record against is chosen from the returned replies (newest preselected). On 200 reload the lanes; on 403/404/409 show the reason in plain words and keep the To Do open.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-23">Scope: `buildWizardItem` passes `sentence` through; when null the wizard keeps its existing Missing statement.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: flip the `lanesBody` test fixture so Not filed is last (the widget still never reorders; keep the test that proves it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 tokens only; light and dark; keyboard reachable. Use the existing dialog/menu components the Worklist already uses; no new shared component.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/059-worklist-widget.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/071-disposition-accrual.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
