  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; load the knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1">Service calls for the GET and POST; picker; sentence pass-through; fixture flip; tests.</step>
    <step order="2">PR into docs/ontology-platform-design.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If 154's merged contract differs from this POML, STOP and report rather than adapting the server.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an inquiry-outcome To Do with replies, when opened, then the picker lists the four dispositions and the replies (newest preselected), and confirming posts `{replyCommunicationId, disposition}` and reloads the lanes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a 403, 404 or 409 (each reason code), then a plain-words message shows and the item stays open.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given any other To Do or a non-To Do subject, then no picker shows and no lookup call is made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a row with a sentence, then the wizard shows it; given null, then the existing Missing statement shows.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no Dataverse or Xrm call from the widget.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests cover the criteria above; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in task notes. The packages build.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

